> Unfortunately, there's no "that's longer than I want it to be" card that
> convinces mixing to happen more quickly: if your model is really going to
> take 1e9 or more updates per step to converge, and if that takes longer
> than 120 hours on your hardware, then that's how long it's going to take.
> If there were magic sauce that could guarantee great convergence with
> minimal computational effort every time, it would already be in the code.
> That said, I don't know that all other options have yet been ruled out;
> and, when folks encounter expensive models on large networks, there are
> various approximate solutions that they may be willing to live with.   But
> if one is working with a dependence model on >=1e4 nodes, one must except
> that one may be in a regime in which gold-standard MCMC-MLE is very
